aints` computation is somehow impacting GKR even though it runs after Round 0 completes. Looking at the flow in `prove_zerocheck_and_logup_gpu`:\n1. GKR input evals (this is where GKR happens)\n2. Fractional sumcheck\n3. Round 0 (this is where my changes apply)\n\nSo Round 0 happens AFTER GKR. My changes to Round 0 can't affect GKR directly because GKR runs first!\n\nUnless... the keygen changes affect GKR. I added `logup_round0_buffer_size` computation to `AirDataGpu::new()`, which is called during keygen. But keygen happens once at startup, not during proving. The proving key is already computed by the time GKR runs.\n\nThe `compute_logup_round0_buffer_size` function is pure CPU logic that builds a DAG and computes rules without any GPU allocation, so it shouldn't impact GPU state. A slightly longer keygen time is unlikely to cause a 184ms regression in GKR performance.\n\nLet me step back and verify the baseline by reverting all my changes and re-running the benchmark to see if GKR consistently returns to 539ms. The before and after measurements were taken at different times, so environmental factors could be at play. I should check which files I've actually modified to see if anything touches GKR directly.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1115,"cache_read_input_tokens":151474,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1115},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0bb129e0-2d55-41ce-bfd8-6ccf294e6721","uuid":"da072510-0007-48d0-8a63-68d38d36bbf1"}
