{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Cd86PqwyyB4uH61Bdi4Emv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ri564BrrD1tPwJeoYajX1N","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nPre-allocate per-thread GPU buffers for Round 0 constraint evaluation\n\nApply the GKR pre-allocation pattern to Round 0: compute max buffer sizes\nacross all AIRs, allocate one set of max-sized buffers per thread, and reuse\nthem across AIRs to eliminate per-AIR cudaMallocAsync/cudaFreeAsync overhead.\n\nChanges:\n- Add Round0ThreadBuffers struct with pre-allocated zerocheck and logup buffers\n- Modify evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu and evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu to\n  accept pre-allocated buffer parameters instead of allocating internally\n- Add compute_logup_round0_buffer_size() helper and cache result in AirDataGpu\n  proving key to avoid expensive per-segment DAG reconstruction\n- Add max-size computation loop and 2GB memory budget safety valve\n\nNote: This optimization regressed performance (Round 0: 296ms -> 443ms at\nAPC 300) due to: (1) AIR batching limits batches to 20-42 items, never\nreaching the >=100 multi-threading threshold; (2) max buffer sizes ~1GB/thread\ndriven by max_temp_bytes; (3) large pre-allocations cause GPU memory pressure\naffecting subsequent phases. Will be reverted.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1","description":"Commit implementation"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":358,"cache_read_input_tokens":172014,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":358},"output_tokens":58,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0bb129e0-2d55-41ce-bfd8-6ccf294e6721","uuid":"865f15ff-3d48-41cc-b0c5-cd68789c59